    "rules": [
      {
        "severity": "required",
        "text": "Keep copper, tracks, vias and other parts out of the antenna zone: the 48 mm wide, 21 mm deep area beyond the module's antenna end, which is part of the footprint's courtyard (KiCad's footprint draws it). Put the antenna end at, or just past, the board edge.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "required",
        "text": "Do not place a ground plane or copper under the antenna part of the module on any layer.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "recommended",
        "text": "The 22 uF and 0.1 uF decoupling capacitors sit at the module's 3V3 pin, on the side away from the antenna.",
        "basis": "convention"
      },
      {
        "severity": "info",
        "text": "Partly routed: the 3V3 decoupling capacitors, the module's ground pin and the EN reset network (pull-up resistor, capacitor, series resistor) are routed on the front layer. The rest is positioned and left as a ratsnest. Route it yourself, with ground pour under and around the module body except at the antenna.",
        "basis": "convention"
      }
    ],
